{
  "_comment": "TM catalog, the compatibility data and the gym leader that awards each TM. A TM teaches its move to a COMPATIBLE Pokemon from the move's min_level on (app/tms.py) - the way past the normal learnset, which only offers the species' level-up moves (app/moves.py, data/learnsets.json). Compatibility follows the games: if the move is a TM in the species' learnset generation (Scarlet/Violet, or the newest game the species was in), the species must learn it by TM there (data/learnsets.json `tm`). For a move that is no TM in that generation, PokeAPI decides: `species.tm_moves` lists every move a species learns from a TM/HM (learn method `machine`, any game), backfilled at startup (tms.backfill) and fetched together with new species (seed.py). Fallback `compatibility`, used while a species has no `tm_moves` yet (offline start, fallback Pokedex) and for every TM listed in `type_based`: the move's type must be one of the Pokemon's own types (already in its learnset) or listed in `type_affinity` for one of its types (a Pokemon takes the union over both types), and a damaging move additionally needs `min_offense` base stat in the stat the move uses (attack for physical, special attack for special), so a Magikarp never learns Earthquake. Mythical Pokemon learn every type-based TM. `type_based`: substitute TMs whose move is no TM in any main-series game (PokeAPI knows no species that learns it by `machine`), see `canonical` of the gyms awarding them - the item keys stay because they live in save data. Single use: teaching consumes the TM, so a TM awarded by several gyms (Rock Tomb) is worth having twice - or, for the ones below, worth buying again. `number` is display only (TM numbers differ per generation, the item key is the move). `canonical` documents the TM the gym leader hands out in the main games; where that move does not exist in data/moves.json, the entry uses the closest available move of the same type and damage class instead. Alola has no gyms (island trials), so it awards no TMs. Rewards per gym: app/rewards.py. Optional `price`: Pokedollar cost in the shop's TM section (app/tms.py catalog_entries, multiplied by shop_price_multiplier like every other item). The buyable set follows Scarlet/Violet, where every TM is obtainable: every SV TM whose move exists in data/moves.json (moves the battle engine lacks - Protect, weather, screens, Hyper Beam, U-turn, ... - are not sold), plus TMs older games sold in department stores/Poke Marts (Celadon, Goldenrod, Alola). A TM with a price may be shop-only (no gym awards it). Price = move power x 100; status moves: self-boosting/healing 10000, status-inflicting 4000, others 5000. TMs without a price stay gym-only rewards.",
